==============================================================================
O14 — residual depth  (fit-free; analytic normalisation only)
==============================================================================
  Delta_N = sum over primes[N:2N] of p^(-sigma) exp(-i t log p)
  envelope (O12, fit-free): |Delta_N| ~ N^(1-sigma)
  g[k,0] = |Delta_N| / N_k^(1-sigma)      N_k = 125 * 2^k
  g[k,d] = g[k,d-1] - g[k-1,d-1]          (backward, along k)
  rho_res = g[k+1,1] / g[k,1]   landmark 2^(-1/2) = 0.70710678
  implied exponent  e = -log2(rho_res)   (e = 0.5 <=> N^(-1/2))
  h_k(theta) = |g[k,1]| * N_k^theta       thetas = [0.25, 0.5, 0.75]
  NOTHING IS FITTED: no least squares, no r^2, no window, no threshold.
  The theta scan is a PARAMETER-FREE SCAN across three FIXED exponents;
  nothing is optimised over theta and no exponent is estimated from data.
  Second normalisation (also analytic, also unfitted):
    a_corr(N) = 1 - sigma*(1 + 1/log(N))
    g_corr[k,0] = |Delta_N| / N_k^(a_corr)
  t = 0 is FIRST and DELIBERATE: the summand is real and non-oscillatory
  there, the closest analogue to the difference table's own object.

  sieving primes to 34000000...
  2089379 primes, largest = 33999967
  ladder N_k = 125 * 2^k, kept while 2N <= n_primes
  ladder kept : [125, 250, 500, 1000, 2000, 4000, 8000, 16000, 32000, 64000, 128000, 256000, 512000, 1024000]
  rungs K = 14
  largest prime index used : 2047999 (value 33283031)
